        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>2.5 “Data Fiduciary/Data Provider”</b> means a person who alone or in
            conjunction with other persons determines the purpose and means of processing
            Personal Data, as defined under the applicable Data Protection Laws, including
            the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023. Each Party shall be an
            independent Data Fiduciary with respect to the Personal Data it processes under
            this Agreement and shall be solely responsible for its own compliance with the
            applicable Data Protection Laws.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            Terms not defined in this Agreement shall have the meanings assigned to them
            under the applicable data protection laws, including the DPDP Act, 2023.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>3. STATUS OF THE PARTIES</b>
        </p>
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>3.1</b> The Parties acknowledge and agree that:
        </p>
        
        <div style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-left:25px;">
            a. Each Party acts as an independent Data Fiduciary;<br/>
            b. Neither Party acts as a Data Processor for the other;<br/>
            c. Each Party shall independently comply with its obligations under the applicable data protection laws, including the DPDP Act;<br/>
            d. Each Party shall independently determine and document its grounds for processing Personal Data in accordance with applicable data protection law;<br/>
            e. Nothing in this Agreement shall be construed to create a joint controllership, partnership, agency, or joint venture between the Parties, and neither Party shall hold itself out as having authority to bind the other Party save as expressly provided in this Agreement.
        </div>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>4. PERSONAL DATA PROCESSING</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>4.1</b> The categories of Personal Data that may be processed include:
        </p>
        
        <table border="0.8px" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="font-size:13px;page-break-inside:avoid;">
            <tr>
                <td style="text-align:center;"><b>Party</b></td>
                <td style="text-align:center;"><b>Categories of Personal Data Processed</b></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Company</td>
                <td>Candidates resume, employee’s details like email and business contacts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Client</td>
                <td>Candidate details and other screening &amp; employment related details</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>4.2</b> The categories of Data Principals include employees.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>4.3</b> Each Party shall ensure that Personal Data shared is adequate,
            relevant, and limited to what is necessary for the specified purposes.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>4.4</b> Each Party shall take reasonable steps to ensure that the Personal
            Data shared under this Agreement is accurate and where necessary kept up to date.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>5. PURPOSE LIMITATION</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>5.1</b> Each Party shall process Personal Data solely for the purpose
            specified in this Agreement or as otherwise permitted under applicable law.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>5.2</b> Neither Party shall process Personal Data in a manner inconsistent
            with the privacy notice provided to the Data Principal or applicable data
            protection law.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>6. PRIVACY NOTICE AND LEGAL BASIS</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>6.1</b> Each Party shall independently comply with applicable transparency
            and notice obligations, including maintaining an up-to-date privacy notice
            describing its processing activities.
        </p>
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>6.2</b> Where consent is required under the DPDP Act, the relevant Party shall:
        </p>
        
        <div style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-left:25px;">
            • Obtain valid consent from the Data Principal;<br/>
            • Maintain records of consent;<br/>
            • Provide a mechanism for withdrawal of consent;<br/>
            • Ensure that withdrawal of consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out prior to such withdrawal, and cease processing the relevant Personal Data for the withdrawn purpose within a reasonable time thereafter, except to the extent processing or retention is otherwise permitted or required by applicable law.
        </div>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>6.3</b> Where processing is based on certain legitimate uses under the DPDP
            Act, each Party shall ensure independent compliance with applicable legal
            requirements.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>7. DATA SECURITY</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>7.1</b> Each Party shall implement appropriate technical and organizational
            measures to safeguard Personal Data.
        </p>
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>7.2</b> Such safeguards may include, at a minimum:
        </p>
        
        <div style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-left:25px;">
            (a) Access controls;<br/>
            (b) Encryption (where appropriate);<br/>
            (c) Authentication mechanisms;<br/>
            (d) Monitoring and incident detection systems;<br/>
            (e) Personnel confidentiality obligations;<br/>
            (f) Periodic review and testing of security measures, where appropriate.
        </div>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>7.3</b> Access to Personal Data shall be restricted to authorized personnel
            on a need-to-know basis.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>7.4</b> Each Party shall comply with requirements of the DPDP Act and
            applicable data protection laws and provide reasonable evidence of its compliance
            with this Agreement, including self-certifications, policy summaries, or
            third-party audit/certification reports and promptly notify the other Party
            following any Personal Data Breach. Nothing in this clause shall require a Party
            to disclose information that is itself confidential to a third party or that
            would compromise its own security.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>8. PERSONAL DATA BREACH</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>8.1</b> In the event of a Personal Data Breach, the affected Party shall
            notify the other Party immediately without undue delay. The Parties shall provide
            all relevant information reasonably required to enable the other Party to assess
            the impact of the Breach and comply with its applicable legal obligations. For
            the avoidance of doubt, the affected Party’s notification obligation to the other
            Party under this Clause 8.1 is independent of, and does not affect, either
            Party’s own obligation to notify the Data Protection Board of India and the
            affected Data Principals in accordance with applicable law.
        </p>
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>8.2</b> The affected Party shall take reasonable steps to:
        </p>
        
        <div style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-left:25px;">
            • Investigate the breach;<br/>
            • Mitigate risks arising from the breach;<br/>
            • Comply with applicable breach notification obligations.
        </div>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>8.3</b> The Parties shall reasonably cooperate with each other in relation
            to any Personal Data Breach affecting the Personal Data shared under this
            Agreement, to the extent necessary to enable each Party to comply with its
            obligations under applicable data protection law.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>8.4</b> The affected Party shall keep the other Party informed of material
            developments relating to the Personal Data Breach where such developments may
            impact the shared Personal Data or the other Party's compliance obligations.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>9. DATA PRINCIPAL RIGHTS</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>9.1</b> Each Party shall independently establish mechanisms to address
            requests from Data Principals.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>9.2</b> Where a request relates to processing carried out by the other Party,
            the receiving Party may redirect the request to the appropriate Party.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>9.3</b> Each Party shall ensure that Data Principals are provided a readily
            available means to submit grievances, and that such grievances are acknowledged
            and addressed within the timelines prescribed under applicable data protection
            laws.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>9.4</b> Each Party shall recognize and give effect to the right of a Data
            Principal to nominate another individual to exercise their rights under the
            DPDP Act, in accordance with Section 14 of the DPDP Act.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>10. RETENTION AND DELETION</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>10.1</b> Each Party shall retain Personal Data only for as long as necessary
            for the specified purpose or as required by law.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>10.2</b> Upon expiry of the retention period, Personal Data shall be deleted
            or anonymized in accordance with applicable legal requirements.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>11. PROCESSORS</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>11.1</b> Each Party shall ensure that any onward sharing of Personal Data
            with a processor is undertaken in compliance with applicable law.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>11.2</b> The Party engaging any processor shall remain responsible for
            ensuring appropriate data protection obligations are imposed on such processor.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>11.3</b> Each Party shall ensure that its contract with any processor is in
            writing and imposes obligations on the processor that are no less protective of
            the Personal Data than the obligations undertaken by such Party under this
            Agreement, including obligations relating to confidentiality, security
            safeguards, and assistance with Data Principal requests and Personal Data Breach
            notifications.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>12. CROSS BORDER DATA TRANSFERS (IF APPLICABLE)</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>12.1</b> Each Party shall independently assess and ensure that any cross
            border transfer undertaken by it complies with applicable legal requirements
            governing such transfers.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>12.2</b> Without prejudice to the generality of Clause 12.1, no Party shall
            transfer Personal Data to any country or territory outside India that has been
            restricted by the Central Government by notification under Section 16 of the
            DPDP Act.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>13. CONFIDENTIALITY</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>13.1</b> Each Party shall maintain confidentiality of Personal Data shared
            under this Agreement.
        </p>
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>13.2</b> Personal Data shall not be disclosed except:
        </p>
        
        <div style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-left:25px;">
            • For the agreed purpose;<br/>
            • As required by applicable law, regulation, court order or regulatory authority;<br/>
            • To authorized personnel and service providers under appropriate safeguards.
        </div>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>14. LIABILITY AND INDEMNITY</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>14.1</b> Each Party shall be independently responsible for its own compliance
            with applicable data protection laws and obligations under this Agreement.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>14.2</b> Each Party shall be responsible for and bear its own losses,
            liabilities, costs, and expenses arising from its breach of this Agreement,
            violation of applicable data protection laws, or failure to implement reasonable
            and appropriate security safeguards.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>14.3</b> Each Party shall indemnify and hold harmless the other Party against
            any losses, damages, liabilities, costs and expenses arising out of or relating
            to its breach of this Agreement or violation of applicable data protection laws.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>14.4</b> A Party seeking indemnification under Clause 14.3 shall:
            (a) promptly notify the other Party in writing of the relevant claim;
            (b) not settle or compromise the claim without the other Party’s prior written
            consent, which is not to be unreasonably withheld; and
            (c) reasonably cooperate with the other Party, at that Party’s expense, in the
            defense of the claim.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>15. SURVIVAL OF OBLIGATIONS UPON TERMINATION</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>15.1</b> Upon termination or expiry of the principal Agreement between the
            Parties, each Party shall, save to the extent retention is required by applicable
            law, delete or return the Personal Data received from the other Party under this
            Agreement within a reasonable time and, on request, certify that it has done so.
            Any obligations relating to confidentiality, security, liability and other
            provisions intended to survive termination shall continue to remain applicable
            as long as the shared Personal Data is retained.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>16. GOVERNING LAW</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>16.1</b> This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance
            with the laws of India, without giving effect to any conflict of laws principles.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>16.2</b> Any dispute, controversy, or claim arising out of or in connection
            with this Agreement, including any question regarding its existence, validity,
            interpretation, performance, breach, termination, or enforcement, shall be
            subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts at Hyderabad,
