        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>18.2</b> A notice shall be deemed to have been duly given:
            (a) when delivered by hand or courier, at the time of delivery;
            (b) when sent by email, at the time of transmission, provided no delivery
            failure notification is received by the sender; or
            (c) when sent by registered post or speed post, five (5) days after the date
            of posting.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19. MISCELLANEOUS</b>
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.1 Entire Agreement:</b> This Agreement along with the principal agreement
            executed between the Parties constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties
            in relation to its subject matter and supersedes all prior discussions,
            understandings, and agreements, whether written or oral, relating to such
            subject matter.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.2 Amendment:</b> No amendment or modification of this Agreement shall be
            effective unless made in writing and signed by the authorized representatives of
            both Parties.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.3 Assignment:</b> Neither Party shall assign, novate, or otherwise transfer
            its rights or obligations under this Agreement without the prior written consent
            of the other Party, save for an assignment to an affiliate or successor in
            connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of substantially all of its
            business, subject to the assignee agreeing in writing to be bound by this
            Agreement.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.4 Severability:</b> If any provision of this Agreement is held to be
            invalid, illegal, or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue in
            full force and effect, and the Parties shall negotiate in good faith to replace
            the invalid provision with a valid provision that most closely reflects the
            original commercial intent.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.5 Waiver:</b> No failure or delay by either Party in exercising any right
            under this Agreement shall operate as a waiver of that right, nor shall any
            single or partial exercise of a right preclude any other or further exercise of
            that right.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.6 Force Majeure:</b> Neither Party shall be liable for any failure or
            delay in the performance of its obligations under this Agreement (other than
            payment obligations) to the extent such failure or delay is caused by
            circumstances beyond its reasonable control, provided that the affected Party
            promptly notifies the other and uses reasonable efforts to mitigate the effect
            of such circumstances. This Clause does not excuse either Party from its
            obligations relating to the security and confidentiality of Personal Data or
            from its obligations to notify a Personal Data Breach.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.7 Counterparts:</b> This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each
            of which shall be deemed an original, and all of which together shall constitute
            one and the same instrument.
        </p>
        
        <p align="justify" style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>19.8 Non-Derogation:</b> Nothing in this Agreement shall be construed to
            limit, reduce, or derogate from either Party’s obligations, or a Data Principal’s
            rights, under the DPDP Act or any other applicable law, and in the event of any
            conflict between this Agreement and the DPDP Act, the DPDP Act shall prevail.
        </p>
        
        
        <p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Times New Roman;">
            <b>EXECUTION</b>
